// As `mutable_cell_has_no_clear_rejected`: one `#[when_unmatched]` line now carries what two arm
// messages carried, so a cell and a non-builder get the same advice with a different 'found'.
//
// The cell is the one mutable type with no `snapshot`, and the message says why rather than listing
// the four that have one: crossing out of a cell is `mutable_get`, an O(1) read, where `snapshot`
// names an O(n) copy of a collection.
fn main() {
    val c = mutable_new(1)
    print(snapshot(c))
}
